# Ghostty, AeroSpace, SketchyBar and JankyBorders are macOS-only here -- the
# closest analog stack to Hyprland/waybar this OS has (no Wayland, so no
# literal port is possible). Nothing on Linux/Windows reads any of these.
#
# Karabiner and the two darwin-*.sh scripts join them for the same reason:
# Karabiner is the left Option -> hyper remap that gives AeroSpace the
# single-key mod SUPER already is on Linux, darwin-key-repeat.sh is the
# NSGlobalDomain half of hypr/input.lua's repeat_rate/repeat_delay, and
# darwin-defaults.sh is the Dock/Finder/Spaces half that has no Linux
# counterpart at all (Hyprland has no Dock to autohide). All macOS-only by
# construction -- Linux does the remap in kb_options and the key repeat in
# input.lua directly.
{{ if ne .chezmoi.os "darwin" }}
.config/ghostty
.config/aerospace
.config/sketchybar
.config/borders
.config/karabiner
darwin-key-repeat.sh
darwin-defaults.sh
{{ end }}
